# Field camera — do not change how the picture is taken

The shutter already works. When fixing the stamp, location text, or where the photo is stored, leave the capture path alone.

## How the picture is taken

- Both buttons open the in-app camera (`PhoneCamera`). Do not switch **Save in the app** back to `<input type="file" capture>`. That picker shows iOS Retake / Use Photo and drops the photo.
- The shutter copies the live video frame onto a canvas at the moment of the tap, then the stamp is painted on that frame.
- **Use phone camera** keeps the file on the phone only (iPhone share sheet, Android download). It does not upload.
- **Save in the app** uploads that same stamped frame to Service360. It does not use the share sheet.

## Stamp on the image

Top to bottom, in this order only:

1. Sydney time
2. Street address
3. Coordinates (`lat, lng`) under the address

Do not put the coordinates above the address. Do not drop the coordinates. Do not stamp placeholder lines such as "Location unavailable".
